---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Evidence" pageSlug="/evidence">

  <!-- ══ HERO ══ -->
  <section class="ev-hero">
    <h1>Everything a program officer would ask for, before you ask.</h1>
    <p class="ev-standfirst">This page exists because we would rather you find our weak spots here than in month three of diligence. Counts, money, governance, and the three things we cannot yet prove.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ 01 WHAT WE COUNT ══ -->
  <section class="ev-counts-section">
    <span class="ev-section-label">01 — What we count</span>
    <h2>The programs, the numbers, and how they are measured.</h2>
    <div class="ev-table-wrap">
      <table class="ev-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Program</th>
            <th>Served</th>
            <th>Sites</th>
            <th>Dosage</th>
            <th>How it is counted</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Read 2 Succeed</td>
            <td class="ev-num">178</td>
            <td class="ev-num">8</td>
            <td>1 hr / week, Jan–Jun</td>
            <td>School enrollment roll</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="ev-table-subrow">
            <td>— of whom completed the year</td>
            <td class="ev-num">173</td>
            <td>—</td>
            <td>97% retention</td>
            <td>End-of-year roll</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>HopeKidz</td>
            <td class="ev-num">65 / wk</td>
            <td class="ev-num">5</td>
            <td>90 min / week, 30 weeks</td>
            <td>Weekly sign-in sheet</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Summer Youth Employment</td>
            <td class="ev-num">24</td>
            <td class="ev-num">1</td>
            <td>25 paid hrs / week, 6 weeks</td>
            <td>NYC SYEP payroll</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>High-school tutoring interns</td>
            <td class="ev-num">37</td>
            <td>—</td>
            <td>Alongside R2S sessions</td>
            <td>Intern roster</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Volunteers signed up</td>
            <td class="ev-num">150</td>
            <td>—</td>
            <td>All background-checked</td>
            <td>Volunteer log</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="ev-partner-schools">
      <strong>Partner Schools</strong>
      Lavelle Preparatory Charter · PS 16 · PS 18 · PS 31 · PS 44 · PS 57 · PS 68 · PS 78
    </p>
    <span class="ev-red-note">[ Retention rate is derived from 178 → 173. Urban Hope to confirm both figures before launch ]</span>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ 02 MEASUREMENT GAP ══ -->
  <section class="ev-gap-section">
    <div class="ev-gap-inner">
      <div class="ev-gap-left">
        <span class="ev-section-label">02 — The measurement gap</span>
        <p class="ev-pull-quote">&ldquo;We can tell you exactly how many children we sat with. We cannot yet tell you, to a standard you should accept, how much their reading improved.&rdquo;</p>
        <p class="ev-gap-body">Our tutors record scores. But our own year-end report prints two different average-growth figures for the same cohort, and mixes a Lexile measure with a reading composite score — two scales that cannot be averaged together. No one outside this office has ever audited any of it.</p>
        <p class="ev-gap-body">We are not going to launder that into a headline number. Here is what we are doing about it instead.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ev-gap-right">
        <div class="ev-step-card">
          <span class="ev-step-label">Step One · This school year</span>
          <p class="ev-step-body">Name the instrument, and use one. Same assessment, administered the same way, at intake and at year end.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ev-step-card">
          <span class="ev-step-label">Step Two</span>
          <p class="ev-step-body">Publish the method in full: instrument, who administers it, dosage actually received, and how many children we lost track of.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ev-step-card">
          <span class="ev-step-label">Step Three · Needs funding</span>
          <p class="ev-step-body">An external evaluator with a comparison group. We have never had one. This is the single most useful thing a funder could buy us.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ 03 MONEY ══ -->
  <section class="ev-money-section">
    <span class="ev-section-label">03 — Money</span>
    <h2>Form 990 figures, as filed.</h2>
    <div class="ev-money-inner">
      <div>
        <div class="ev-990-table-wrap">
          <table class="ev-990-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>FY</th>
                <th>Revenue</th>
                <th>Expenses</th>
                <th>Net assets</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>2023</td>
                <td>$800,510</td>
                <td>$713,638</td>
                <td>$626,346</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>2022</td>
                <td>$844,033</td>
                <td>$719,913</td>
                <td>$539,474</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>2021</td>
                <td>$610,460</td>
                <td>$378,623</td>
                <td>$415,354</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>2020</td>
                <td class="ev-no-filing" colspan="3">No filing on record — explained in the packet</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>2019</td>
                <td>$276,928</td>
                <td>$242,269</td>
                <td>$59,363</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>2018</td>
                <td>$130,728</td>
                <td>$173,138</td>
                <td>$24,704</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ev-money-panels">
        <!-- Open question panel -->
        <div class="ev-money-panel ev-money-panel-amber">
          <span class="ev-panel-label">FY2023 — we amended this return</span>
          <p class="ev-panel-body">We filed our 2023 return in October 2024 and amended it in February 2025, because contribution revenue and program expenses had both been reported incorrectly. The figures on the left are from the amended return — the one that stands. The original showed a $460,313 deficit that was not real.</p>
          <p class="ev-panel-body"><strong>Some public databases still serve the withdrawn figures. If you are looking at a 2023 deficit for us, you have the superseded return. The amended one is in the packet.</strong></p>
        </div>
        <!-- Officer compensation panel -->
        <div class="ev-money-panel">
          <span class="ev-panel-label">Officer Compensation · FY2023</span>
          <div class="ev-panel-row">
            <span>President &amp; Founder</span>
            <span class="ev-panel-row-val">$44,000</span>
          </div>
          <div class="ev-panel-row">
            <span>Executive Director</span>
            <span class="ev-panel-row-val">$44,000</span>
          </div>
          <div class="ev-panel-row">
            <span>All other salaries</span>
            <span class="ev-panel-row-val">$99,350</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <!-- Largest funders panel -->
        <div class="ev-money-panel">
          <span class="ev-panel-label">Largest Institutional Funders</span>
          <ul class="ev-funder-list">
            <li>National Christian Charitable Foundation</li>
            <li>Hope for New York</li>
            <li>The Minneapolis Foundation</li>
            <li>The Staten Island Foundation</li>
            <li>NYC DYCD</li>
          </ul>
          <span class="ev-red-note">[ Amounts and periods to confirm ]</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Governance flags row -->
    <div class="ev-flag-row">
      <div class="ev-flag-card">
        <span class="ev-flag-status">Not yet in place</span>
        <p class="ev-flag-title">Independent audit</p>
        <p class="ev-flag-body">None. We have never commissioned one. Charity Navigator flags this publicly, and they are right to.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ev-flag-card">
        <span class="ev-flag-status">Not yet in place</span>
        <p class="ev-flag-title">Records retention policy</p>
        <p class="ev-flag-body">Drafted, not yet adopted by the board. Also a live Charity Navigator flag.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ev-flag-card">
        <span class="ev-flag-status ev-flag-status-amber">Not yet on this page</span>
        <p class="ev-flag-title">Program vs admin split</p>
        <p class="ev-flag-body">The amended return breaks expenses into program, management and fundraising. It belongs here, with our own explanation beside it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ 04 GOVERNANCE ══ -->
  <section class="ev-gov-section">
    <span class="ev-section-label">04 — Governance</span>
    <h2>The board, the policies, and the conflicts we will name ourselves.</h2>
    <div class="ev-gov-inner">
      <div>
        <div class="ev-gov-stats">
          <div class="ev-gov-figure-row">
            <span class="ev-gov-num">9</span>
            <span class="ev-gov-caption">directors on the board</span>
          </div>
          <div class="ev-gov-figure-row">
            <span class="ev-gov-num">2</span>
            <span class="ev-gov-caption">of whom are also staff</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="ev-gov-body">Our founder and our executive director both sit on the board. That is a real independence question and we would rather name it than have you raise it. The board roster, bios, and outside affiliations are in the packet.</p>
        <span class="ev-red-note">[ Board roster + bios — Urban Hope to supply; names published here only with their consent ]</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <table class="ev-policy-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Policy</th>
              <th>Status</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Conflict of interest</td>
              <td><span class="ev-status-green">In place</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Child protection &amp; background checks</td>
              <td><span class="ev-status-green">In place</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Whistleblower policy</td>
              <td><span class="ev-status-amber">Drafted</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Records retention</td>
              <td><span class="ev-status-red">Not adopted</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Independent financial audit</td>
              <td><span class="ev-status-red">None</span></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <span class="ev-red-note">[ Every status here to be confirmed by Urban Hope before launch ]</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ 05 DOCUMENTS ══ -->
  <section class="ev-docs-section">
    <span class="ev-section-label">05 — Documents</span>
    <h2>Everything in one place.</h2>
    <span class="ev-docs-note">No form, no gate.</span>
    <div class="ev-docs-grid">
      <div class="ev-doc-card">
        <span class="ev-doc-badge">PDF</span>
        <p class="ev-doc-title">Form 990</p>
        <span class="ev-doc-years">2021, 2022, 2023 (as amended)</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ev-doc-card">
        <span class="ev-doc-badge">PDF</span>
        <p class="ev-doc-title">End-of-year reports</p>
        <span class="ev-doc-years">2023, 2024, 2025</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ev-doc-card">
        <span class="ev-doc-badge">PDF</span>
        <p class="ev-doc-title">Current-year budget</p>
        <span class="ev-doc-years">With the funding gap stated</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ev-doc-card">
        <span class="ev-doc-badge">PDF</span>
        <p class="ev-doc-title">IRS determination letter</p>
        <span class="ev-doc-years">501(c)(3) · April 2011</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
